{
  "id": "winter-challenge-2007",
  "name": "Winter Challenge 2007",
  "category": "event",
  "description": {
    "text": "The Winter Challenge was a free event at eight venues across Japan on eleven days from 25 November 2007 to 20 January 2008, with corners for every level of player. Every visitor got Leafeon 069/DP-P inside the event's play guide booklet. The main tournament, the Challenge Arena, gave its players Glaceon 070/DP-P; there two wins in a row earned a point, three points won a cosmos holo Time-Space Distortion and seven points a Mysterious Pearl, both first given out at Battle Road 2007.\n\nInfernape LV.X 071/DP-P went to players of Challenge the Gym Leaders and Team Galactic, against staff playing the characters of Diamond & Pearl. Beginners had their own corners: the First Battle gave Grotle, Monferno or Prinplup, the Trade Challenge Magmar and the Battle Challenge Electabuzz, all cards first given out in Trade Please DP swaps at Pokémon Center stores that year, and children who took the paid First Classroom DP lesson got Turtwig, Chimchar or Piplup 072-074/DP-P for their class.",
